{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL builders (fetcher.py)","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status = Done","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","jql","status category","active set","done scope","workflow","custom status"],"propositions":["The reconciler hardcodes status != 'Done' to scope the active set, which fails for client workflows with custom closed-equivalent statuses (Closed/Resolved/Cancelled) that are not literal 'Done' status.","Issues in custom closed statuses are incorrectly pulled into jql_active as active work, causing the reconciler to treat resolved issues as active and potentially push mutations at them.","jql_done_recent misses custom closed statuses and fails to populate the recent-Done snapshot, mis-scoping the entire active set for non-DIG/REB workflows.","The fix switches the Done predicate from literal status = 'Done' to Jira's workflow-agnostic statusCategory = Done / statusCategory != Done, which correctly maps all custom closed statuses."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786827393745529001,"uuid":"3efe134a-7d6a-42bd-9b16-c0f87627517b"}